  "presentation_summary": [
    "Previously healthy 36-year-old man presented with four days of fever, headache, generalized body aches, sore throat and voice change, followed by dysphagia and bilateral upper neck pain.",
    "On examination he was alert but dehydrated, irritable and hypotensive with blood pressure 101/39 mmHg, heart rate 133/min, respiratory rate 22/min, temperature 38.7 C, oxygen saturation 97% on room air and GCS 14/15.",
    "Pharynx was markedly congested with enlarged tonsils nearly obstructing the airway; no rash, petechiae or purpura were present at initial examination.",
    "Admission labs showed WBC 18.3 x10^3/uL, platelets 33 x10^3/uL, CRP 179 mg/L, PCT >100 ng/mL, creatinine 255 umol/L, potassium 2.8 mmol/L, sodium 131 mmol/L, ALT 675 U/L, AST 584 U/L, bilirubin 38 umol/L, PT 22.9 s, INR 2.0, APTT 64.4 s, D-dimer 125.9 mg/L FEU, CK 3025 U/L, myoglobin 3405 ng/mL, lactate 13.4 mmol/L."
  ],
